WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.900
Mist on the marshes.

2
00:00:01.950 --> 00:00:05.060
A small boy runs, clutching a parcel.

3
00:00:05.110 --> 00:00:08.460
Gates and posts loom out
of the mist, shouting:

4
00:00:08.510 --> 00:00:10.570
"A boy with somebody else’s pork pie!

5
00:00:10.620 --> 00:00:11.930
Stop him!"

6
00:00:11.980 --> 00:00:14.890
On the river, a dark prison ship.

7
00:00:14.940 --> 00:00:19.850
Years later, he brushes dust off
a fine coat outside a prison wall.

8
00:00:19.900 --> 00:00:22.080
He never commits a real crime.

9
00:00:22.130 --> 00:00:24.940
So why does Pip feel so guilty?

10
00:00:24.990 --> 00:00:28.420
In this mission, you'll
enter a harsh world of crime:

11
00:00:28.470 --> 00:00:35.240
prison hulks, used from 1776 to 1857,
and convicts shipped to Australia.

12
00:00:35.290 --> 00:00:38.720
You'll follow a stolen pie, and
the silence that follows it,

13
00:00:38.770 --> 00:00:40.770
from the very first chapters.

14
00:00:40.820 --> 00:00:45.090
And you'll watch two convicts with
the same crimes face the court.

15
00:00:45.140 --> 00:00:48.920
Your mission: explain
why Pip feels so guilty.
